          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "थाटणे — thāṭṇe — \"to set up; to lay out with care\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विणकराने बाजारात नवीन दुकान थाटलं. viṇkarāne bājārāt navīn dukān thāṭlaṁ. The weaver set up a new shop in the market."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with -ने (he …): त्याने दुकान थाटलं, tyāne dukān thāṭlaṁ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "थाटणे (thāṭṇe) is said of a shop or a home set up with some show; थाट is the show itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "थाटणे (thāṭṇe) is built on थाट, \"pomp, a fine arrangement\"; CDIAL sets Hindi ṭhāṭh, \"pomp\", and Marathi thaṭṇẽ, \"to act pompously\", under thaṭṭha, \"pomp, ceremony\" (CDIAL 6090)."
            }
          ]
        },
